            {
              "id": "998de115-6f83-368a-9a3d-09d99dd85b53",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible undefined behavior risk due to overlapping memory regions between the source and destination buffers in the strncpy operation. The source and destination may refer to overlapping memory, which is not allowed by the C standard for strncpy and can result in unpredictable behavior. Additionally, there are no explicit checks ensuring that the source and destination are non-null, which increases the risk of null pointer dereference. The absence of a guard for buffer sizes and the lack of explicit null-termination after the copy further increase the risk. The analysis also found that the source and destination may be related via data flow, which makes overlap feasible. All these factors indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue that should be remediated.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the undefined behavior risk caused by possible overlapping memory regions in the strncpy operation, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap before performing the copy. Additionally, add explicit null pointer checks for both the source and destination pointers to prevent null pointer dereference. After copying, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer to avoid unterminated strings.\n\nExample fix:\n\n```cpp\nif (fw_version && fw_version->version && buf) {\n    // Ensure source and destination do not overlap\n    if ((fw_version->version + AGA_MAX_STR_LEN <= buf) || (buf + AGA_MAX_STR_LEN <= fw_version->version)) {\n        strncpy(fw_version->version, buf, AGA_MAX_STR_LEN);\n        fw_version->version[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n    } else {\n        // Handle overlap error\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis approach checks for null pointers, verifies that the buffers do not overlap, and ensures the destination is null-terminated after the copy.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS111237"
                ]
              }
