            {
              "id": "45b23a69-1881-3295-bc69-5c7a3eaf6efe",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the strncpy operation. The dataflow analysis suggests that the destination and source may refer to overlapping memory, which is not allowed by the C standard for strncpy and can result in unpredictable program behavior. Additionally, there are no explicit checks to ensure that the source and destination are non-null, increasing the risk of null pointer dereference. The absence of a guard for buffer boundaries and the lack of explicit null-termination further increase the risk. These factors indicate a real and actionable security or correctness issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the undefined behavior risk caused by possible overlapping memory regions in the strncpy operation, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap before performing the copy. If overlap is possible, use a temporary buffer to safely copy the data. Additionally, add explicit null pointer checks for both source and destination pointers to prevent null dereference. Finally, ensure the destination buffer is null-terminated after the copy to avoid unterminated strings.\n\nExample fix:\n\n```cpp\nif (status && vbios_info.part_number && status->vbios_part_number != vbios_info.part_number) {\n    char temp[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN];\n    strncpy(temp, vbios_info.part_number, AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1);\n    temp[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1] = '\\0';\n    strncpy(status->vbios_part_number, temp, AGA_MAX_STR_LEN);\n    status->vbios_part_number[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\nThis approach ensures that the source and destination do not overlap, prevents null pointer dereference, and guarantees null-termination of the destination buffer.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS111237"
                ]
              }
